=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/IncidentTimeline (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/IncidentTimeline   kind=page   web route=/system-status/incidents/:id
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/IncidentTimelinePage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every routed feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure Microsoft.UI-free records +
  projection + registration + diagnostics, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client data
  adapter), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (the observable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated
  prompt's idealized "IncidentTimelinePage.xaml + IncidentTimelinePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/System"
  is mapped onto these real conventions — exactly as the W7 ChargingDetailPage / MyActivityPage precedents are.
- Namespace: TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (matching RouteGroup.SystemOps in Core/Navigation/RouteTable.cs,
  where Hidden("IncidentTimeline","system-status/incidents/:id",RouteGroup.SystemOps,"Incident") already exists),
  NOT a ".System" leaf (a literal "System" namespace shadows the global System namespace for sibling files —
  the same decision the MyActivityPage W7 log records). The incident severity/status unions (IncidentSeverity /
  IncidentStatus + wire mappings) are the incident-domain authority already declared once for the parent
  TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews namespace in IncidentForm.Model.cs; this page consumes them (resolved from the parent
  namespace) rather than re-declaring them — no CS0101 duplicate type.
- Three data sources = the web page's three hooks, names kept at the C# call sites:
    useIncident            -> GET   /status/incidents/{id}          op get_api_v1_status_incidents_id
    useAppendIncidentUpdate-> POST  /status/incidents/{id}/updates  op post_api_v1_status_incidents_id_updates
    usePatchIncident       -> PATCH /status/incidents/{id}          op patch_api_v1_status_incidents_id
  IncidentTimelineClientSource binds the generated C# client (ADR-004) for the read + both writes, parses every
  incident envelope through the tolerant IncidentDetail/IncidentUpdateItem readers (snake_case, null-tolerant),
  and classifies any fault through the shared ApiErrorMapper rather than throwing — so a 404 becomes the
  never-blank not-found surface and a write fault becomes a toast (web parity: the mutation resolves to a toast,
  never an unhandled rejection). The operation ids were cross-checked against the generated endpoint table in
  apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs. EmptyIncidentTimelineSource is the shell default (renders the
  not-found surface until a host wires the client source via IncidentTimelinePage.Create — the same deferred
  wiring as the sibling detail pages). Registered in ShellWindow.xaml.cs PageFactory under "IncidentTimeline"
  (the RouteTable nav name), reading the route :id via ParseSessionId(_viewModel.Current.Param("id")) and mapping
  the in-body back affordance to NavigateTo("system-status").
- The view composes the shared PageContainer chrome (title = incident.title / "Incident"; subtitle =
  "Incident #id" / "Loading…" / "Not found"; a Back action in the actions slot; PageContainer.IsLoading drives
  the loading spinner — web loading branch) around the four web GlassPanels, each a Fluent TsGlassPanel built
  from W2 design tokens: GlassPanel1 (not-found / web error||!incident branch), GlassPanel2 (header: severity
  glyph tinted by tone, status TsBadge, severity label, source, open/resolved-duration TsBadge, description,
  affected-components line, started/resolved meta and the Resolve TsButton), GlassPanel3 (newest-first update
  timeline — [...updates].reverse() — each a status TsBadge + absolute timestamp + optional "· author" + the
  message on a left rail) and GlassPanel4 (append form: TsTextarea + status TsSelect + Add TsButton, hidden once
  resolved). The resolve action is gated behind a TsConfirmDialog (web ConfirmDialog) and both writes raise an
  InfoBar toast (web useToast). All branch selection, fmtDuration tiers, the STATUS_BADGE / SEVERITY_TONE /
  STATUS_LABEL tables and i18n happen in the Microsoft.UI-free IncidentTimelineProjection; the view is a thin
  renderer with coalesced UI-thread marshalling.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal flows through the ILocalizer facade via IncidentTimelineStrings keys with
  the web literal as the English fallback (the established IncidentForm / IncidentsCard pattern — the platform
  Strings/*.resw catalog is generator-owned by apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts and is NOT hand-edited;
  Localization.Get / PassthroughLocalizer resolve a missing key to the fallback, so the page renders correctly
  and stays format/drift-clean). Lifecycle status + severity labels reuse the shared status.incidents.status.* /
  status.incidents.severity.* keys (single-sourced with IncidentForm / IncidentsCard); page-specific copy is
  keyed under status.incidentTimeline.*. A RecordingLocalizer test asserts every projected string routes through
  a catalogued key.
- a11y (ADR-015): the page, each panel, the toast and every interactive element carry AutomationProperties
  names/ids; the surface adds no bespoke motion so reduced-motion is honoured by construction; light/dark + high
  contrast come from the tokenized shared components. SI units: N/A — this surface carries no unit-bearing fields
  (durations are wall-clock deltas formatted by the shared port). PII-safe diagnostics emit only
  "view.opened / status.incident.update.appended / status.incident.resolved slug=IncidentTimelinePage" — never an
  incident title, description, component or update body.
- The AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer the web page renders between the header and the timeline is a SEPARATE
  component parity unit (gated by withAiFeature; renders null when AI is off, which is the default surface). It is
  out of this page unit's scope and not built here.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=6

# Panels (4) — every web GlassPanel reproduced as a Fluent TsGlassPanel from W2 tokens (never blank; ADR-011)
[x] panel  - GlassPanel1  -> IncidentTimelinePage.cs _notFoundPanel (TsGlassPanel, AutomationId "incident-timeline-not-found"); BuildBody hosts _notFoundText (web "Incident {id} not found or you don't have access.") + the Back-to-System-Status TsButton; shown in the NotFound state (web error || !incident branch). Projection: IncidentTimelineProjection.Project NotFound branch (IncidentTimelineStrings.NotFound, id embedded); test Project_not_found_branch_embeds_the_route_id
[x] panel  - GlassPanel2  -> IncidentTimelinePage.cs _headerPanel (TsGlassPanel "incident-timeline-header") built by BuildHeaderPanel: severity FontIcon tinted via StatusResources.AccentBrushKey(display.SeverityTone), status TsBadge, severity label, source Caption, open/resolved-duration TsBadge, description Text, affects Caption, Clock meta Caption and the Resolve TsButton. Projection: Project Ready branch + RenderHeader; tests Project_ready_branch_projects_open_header_timeline_and_form / Project_resolved_incident_hides_open_badge_and_uses_success_tone
[x] panel  - GlassPanel3  -> IncidentTimelinePage.cs _timelinePanel (TsGlassPanel "incident-timeline-updates") built by BuildTimelinePanel: Message glyph + "Timeline" PanelTitle + "{n} entries" Caption, and _timelineList rebuilt by RenderTimeline from display.Rows (BuildTimelineRow → status TsBadge + absolute timestamp + optional "· author" + message on a left rail). Projection: IncidentTimelineProjection.BuildRows reverses oldest-first to newest-first; test BuildRows_reverses_updates_newest_first_with_author_and_status
[x] panel  - GlassPanel4  -> IncidentTimelinePage.cs _formPanel (TsGlassPanel "incident-timeline-form") built by BuildFormPanel: TsTextarea (MaxLength 4000) + status TsSelect (5 web options) + Add TsButton; RenderForm hides it once resolved (web {!isResolved && …}). Projection: IncidentTimelineProjection.BuildStatusOptions; tests BuildStatusOptions_keeps_current_then_four_targets / ViewModel_append_success_clears_form_and_applies_refreshed_incident

# Data states (2 manifest-declared: loading, success) — plus the web not-found branch, each a visible region
[x] state  - loading      -> IncidentTimelineState.Loading; IncidentTimelineProjection.Project loading branch sets Display.IsLoading=true → IncidentTimelinePage.Render sets PageContainer.IsLoading=true (web loading spinner replaces the body); IncidentTimelinePageViewModel starts Loading and LoadAsync keeps it until the first read resolves; tests Project_loading_branch_shows_spinner_subtitle / ViewModel_starts_in_the_loading_state
[x] state  - success      -> IncidentTimelineState.Ready (web success branch); Project Ready branch emits the header/timeline/form display; IncidentTimelinePage.Render shows _successStack (GlassPanel2+3+4); IncidentTimelinePageViewModel.LoadAsync enters Ready on a loaded incident and stamps UpdatedAt; tests Project_ready_branch_projects_open_header_timeline_and_form / ViewModel_load_success_enters_ready_and_stamps_updated_at
# (the web page additionally branches not-found — implemented as GlassPanel1 above + ViewModel_load_failure_enters_not_found; the two writes are covered by ViewModel_append_* / ViewModel_resolve_* and the contract-client ClientSource_* tests.)

